    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a CAPABILITY and not an artifact: restoration conditions expressed as a resolvable citation to an executing consumer rather than as prose, so a promise naming no route fails to compile — writing this particular sentence better retires nothing.)",

    "**SECOND SPECIMEN, AND IT MOVES THE CLASS FROM A WITHHOLD TO A GREEN-BY-EXECUTION RECEIPT, measured 2026-09-05 at head 4da9c1a3fdd.** The subject here is not a suppressed expected-red but the repository's WEAK SELF-HOST BEHAVIORAL RECEIPT: `test.claim.self_host_logic_behavioral_witness` `self_host_logic_behavioral_receipt_holds`, whose transport `tools.self_host_logic_behavioral_transport` emits `dag/std/logic.dag` with the real `gunbc` binary, compiles the emitted Rust against the seed crate, and runs the resulting binary plain and `--inject-fault` — DESIGN section 7 equivalence-by-execution with its own discriminating RED, landed as Wave 1 Gate 4. IT IS CLASSIFIED ONTO A CADENCE THAT EXECUTES NOTHING: `FalsifierSelfHostWet`, whose sole scheduled executor `falsifier.yml` was deleted at 611fd02770 (#8283, 2026-08-15); `std.witness_admission` `witness_cadence_has_scheduled_route` answers false for it, and the tree is CORRECT about this at every carrier — the witness file says so in its own header, `v2.compiler.self_host.wet_receipt_enrollment` records the cadence flag's deletion, and `gunbc.deleted_cadence_reference_census` censuses it as PremiseInvalidated. WHAT MAKES IT THIS CLASS RATHER THAN AN HONEST DARK LANE: the classification is not a promise of restoration in prose, it is a LIVE ROUTING DECISION that names a cadence the tree does not contain, and the receipt it routes is CITED AS COVERAGE ELSEWHERE — `docs/plans/v2-self-hosting.md` lists Wave 1 gate 4 as RECEIPT LANDED. A landed receipt with no executor is the inert-lens state DESIGN section 4b names worse than absent, and the citation is what stops anyone looking, exactly as this row's first specimen describes. THE BOUNDARY THAT KEPT IT UNFILED: every carrier is individually honest — nobody claims the cadence runs — so a reader auditing any ONE of them finds a correct statement, and only the JOIN of `this receipt is cited as gate coverage` with `this cadence has no route` is false. Restoring a scheduled route for the cadence is reserved to operator agreement by `std.witness_admission` `witness_cadence_has_scheduled_route_note`, so the repair is not a lane's to take unilaterally, which is why the standing must be visible here rather than resolved quietly.)",

    "**THIRD SPECIMEN: A REFUSAL WHOSE REMEDY NAMES A LANE THAT CANNOT TAKE THE WITNESS, measured 2026-10-03 on gunbc#13103 (advisories step 2).** When a changed witness is interrupted at the wall deadline, `v1_compiler.cli_run.required_floor_runner` prints `Reduce the cost, or move it to a lane declaring its own ceiling, so the witness reaches a verdict.` For a witness in a LONG home that route does not exist: `v2.workflow.required_floor` `changed_witness_cost_policy` runs every changed witness whose expensiveness is declared (`changed_witness_expensiveness_is_declared`: the cost-debt roster OR `long_home_prefixes`) under `ChangedCostDebtVerdictOnly`, which observes the CPU line but keeps the 8s WALL ARMED. The long home IS the lane declaring the expense, and it carries no ceiling of its own, so the refusal sends the author to the place the witness already is.",

    "THE CONSEQUENCE, AND THE POPULATION IT STRANDS: a long-home witness whose cost exceeds the wall can never be EDITED. Any edit force-runs it into the wall, and leaving it unedited leaves its pins stale. Live specimen: `v2.test.long.compile_door_ledger` `ledger_cause_histogram_over_mixed_affected_set` pins head-grain counts (`ledger_cause_count` of `parse_grammar_choice_overlap_residue` == 1, of `resolve_reason_unbound_symbol` == 2) that are false once the door ledger counts FATAL causes (advisories step 2). The correct fatal-grain counts, by real execution of `v2.test.long.compile_door_ledger` `affected_rows` on head f058676e6f: `resolve_reason_unbound_symbol` 1 (dag/std/determinism.dag), `member_not_a_binder` 2 (dag/std/error_primitives.dag, dag/std/bit.dag), residue 0, `all_refused_causes_attributed` true. THE CLAIM STAYS UNEDITED, AND RED ON ITS STALE PINS, BY RULING (sharp-raven-357, 2026-10-03): a one-time override to land an edit through the wall is the DESIGN section 5 escape hatch, so the restructure waits for a ceiling-bearing route. That restructure is the three-subject histogram as the supplied-chain claim `v2.test.claim.advisories.fatal_first_readers` `door_ledger_histogram_counts_each_refusals_fatal_holds` (which landed with step 2) plus one single-subject real-route claim in the long module. It was measured: a trivial baseline took 180s wall and the single-subject door route on dag/std/bit.dag took 765s wall in the same run (head 11b5bd23f4), so the claim alone costs about 585s against the 8s wall. sharp-raven-357 is raising the ceiling-bearing CI lane with the operator, and the re-pin is owned by the advisories lane (bold-lynx-438)",

